      en: "Oistins is a town on the south coast of Barbados, known for its vibrant nightlife and fish market. The name derives from an English nobleman, Sir John Oistin. Historically an important fishing port, it is now a hub for tourists and locals. Oistins is famous for the 'Oistins Fish Fry', held every Friday evening, offering a wide variety of grilled fish and seafood. The town also features a historic fort, Fort Charles, from the 17th century. Oistins has a population of about 2,500 residents. Nearby beaches, such as Miami Beach, are popular for water sports.",
