      en: "Belleplaine is a village in the parish of Saint Andrew, Barbados, located on the northeast coast of the island. It is a rural settlement with an agricultural character, surrounded by sugarcane fields and hills. Belleplaine has a small population of about 500 residents. The village is near the Scotland District, a region with unique geology and eroded hills. Belleplaine offers stunning views of the Atlantic Ocean and is a quiet place away from tourist crowds. The economy is mainly based on agriculture and fishing. Nearby are hiking trails and nature paths.",
