      en: "Crab Hill is a village in the parish of Saint Lucy, Barbados, located about 2 km inland from the northern coast. It emerged from a sugar plantation established in the 1720s. The settlement now serves as a residential area for workers in nearby Speightstown. Crab Hill has a small primary school and a community center. The village covers approximately 1.2 km² and sits at an elevation of 60 meters above sea level. Annual rainfall averages 1,300 mm. The population was recorded at 812 in the 2010 census.",
