      en: "Bentleys is a small settlement on the east coast of Barbados, in Saint John parish, perched on a cliff overlooking the Atlantic. Population is about 250. The area has steep terrain and lush vegetation. Ruins of an old sugar mill are a notable landmark. The economy is agricultural and tourism-related, with vacation rentals. Bathsheba is 2 km north. Annual rainfall is high at 1,800 mm due to the windward coast.",
